---one through each of the two original vertices it is adjacent to. One of thes
e has to be broken to create a uniconnected subgraph. How could we break it? We
 could pick one of these two vertices to disconnect from the sink by deleting e
ither arc $(x, s)$ or $(y, s)$ for new vertex $v_{xy}$. We maximize the size of
 our subgraph by finding the smallest number of arcs to delete. We must delete 
the outgoing arc from at least one of the two vertices defining each original e
dge. \emph{But this is exactly the same as finding the vertex cover in this gra
ph!} The reduction is illustrated in Figure 11.8. 
