 the DFS tree $T$ form a vertex cover? Recall that the magic property of depth-
first search is that it partitions all edges into tree edges and back edges. If
 a vertex $v$ is a leaf of $T$, then there is a single tree edge $(x, v)$ conta
ining it, which will be covered by taking non-leaf vertex $x$. If there are oth
er edges containing $v$, they must be back edges going to ancestors of $v$, all
 of which were selected to be in the cover. So all edges will be covered by the
 set of non-leaves. 
