a probability distribution. Each of the $2^{n}$ bit patterns has an associated 
probability, where $p(i)$ is the probability that when the machine is read, it 
would report being in state $i$. This probability distribution is much richer t
han with conventional deterministic machines: there can be a non-zero probabili
ty of being in all $N$ states at any given time. Being able to manipulate proba
bility distribution in parallel for all $N = 2^{n}$ states is the real win of q
uantum computing. As is true of any probability distribution, all these probabi
lities must sum to one, so $\sum_{i=0}^{N-1} p(i)=1$.\index{consulting services
} 
