Overfull \hbox (2395.49203pt too wide) in paragraph at lines 10717--10717
[]\T1/lmtt/m/it/10 The key to algorithm design (or any other problem-solving ta
sk) is to proceed by asking yourself questions to guide your thought process. W
hat if we do this? What if we do that? Should you get stuck on the problem, the
 best thing to do is move onto the next question. In any group brainstorming se
ssion, the most useful person in the room is the one who keeps asking Why cant 
we do it this way?; not the nitpicker who keeps telling them why. Because he or
 she will eventually stumble on an approach that cant be shot down. 
 []

