[]\T1/lmtt/m/it/10 Finally, I have a confession to make. For several years, I s
erved as Chief Scientist at a startup company named General Sentiment, and inte
rviewed all the developers we hired. Most of them knew me as the author of this
 book, and feared they were in for a grilling. But I never asked them a single 
algorithm puzzle question. We needed developers who could wrangle a complicated
 distributed system, not solve puzzles. I asked a lot of questions about the bi
ggest program they had worked on and what they did with it, in order to get a s
ense of the sophistication of what they could handle and what they liked to do.
 I am very proud of the excellent people we hired at General Sentiment, all of 
whom have gone on to even more exciting places.\index{bipartite matching}\index
{Fibonacci heap}\index{pairing heap} 
