epresented using a linked list, array, or dictionary containing exactly the ele
ments in $S$. No notion of a fixed universal set is needed for such a data stru
cture. Dictionaries can be more space and time efficient for sparse subsets tha
n bit vectors, and easier to work with. For efficient union and intersection op
erations, it pays to keep the elements in each subset sorted, so a linear-time 
merge of both subsets identifies all duplicates. 
