Overfull \hbox (2941.49045pt too wide) in paragraph at lines 11355--11355
[]\T1/lmtt/m/it/10 \item \emph{Is my system sparse?} A key to recognizing that 
you have a special-case linear system is establishing how many matrix elements 
you really need to describe $A$. If there are only a few non-zero elements, you
r matrix is \emph{sparse} and you are in luck. If these few non-zero elements a
re clustered near the diagonal, your matrix is \emph{banded} and you are in eve
n more luck. Algorithms for reducing the bandwidth of a matrix are discussed in
 Section 16.2. Many other regular patterns of sparse matrices can also be explo
ited, so consult the manual of your solver or a good book on numerical analysis
 for details. 
 []


