$ such that $A[i, k]=A[k, j]=1$, so $i$ to $k$ to $j$ is a path of length 2 in 
$G$. More generally, $A^{k}[i, j]$ counts the number of paths of length exactly
 $k$ between $i$ and $j$. This count includes non-simple paths, where vertices 
are repeated, such as $i$ to $k$ to $i$ to $j$. 
