Overfull \hbox (4747.4852pt too wide) in paragraph at lines 12075--12075
[]\T1/lmtt/m/it/10 \item \emph{Might access frequencies change over time?} --- 
Reordering a list or tree to exploit a skewed access pattern requires knowing t
he access pattern in advance. For many applications, it can be difficult to obt
ain this information. Better are \emph{self-organizing lists}, where the order 
of the keys changes in response to the queries. The best self-organizing scheme
 is move-to-front; that is, we move the most recently searched-for key from its
 current position to the front of the list. Popular keys keep getting boosted t
o the front, while unsearched-for keys drift towards the back of the list. Ther
e is no need to keep track of the frequency of access; just move the keys on de
mand. Self-organizing lists also exploit \emph{locality of reference}, since ac
cesses to any given key are likely to occur in clusters. A hot key will be main
tained near the top of the list during its cluster of accesses, even if other k
eys have proven more popular in the past. 
 []


