[]\T1/lmtt/m/it/10 Self-organization can extend the useful size range of sequen
tial search, although you should switch to binary search beyond one hundred ele
ments. But consider using \emph{splay trees}, which are self-organizing binary 
search trees that rotate each searched-for node to the root. They offer excelle
nt amortized performance guarantees. 
