[]\T1/lmtt/m/it/10 By definition, the relative order among the elements does no
t distinguish different subsets. Thus, $\{1,2,5\}$ is the same as $\{2,1,5\}$. 
However, it is a very good idea to maintain your subsets in a sorted or \textit
{canonical} order to speed up operations such as testing whether or not two sub
sets are identical. 
