[]\T1/lmtt/m/it/10 To generate a random subset, you could try to generate a ran
dom integer from 0 to $2^{n}-1$ and unrank, although your random number generat
or might round things off in a way certain subsets can never occur. Much better
 is to flip a coin $n$ times, with the $i$th flip deciding whether to include e
lement $i$ in the subset. A coin flip can be robustly simulated by generating a
 random real or large integer and testing whether it is bigger or smaller than 
half its range. 
