[]\T1/lmtt/m/it/10 The best theoretical bounds on finding minimum spanning tree
s tell a complicated story. Karger, Klein, and Tarjan [KKT95] give a linear-tim
e randomized algorithm for MSTs, based again on Borukvas algorithm. Chazelle [C
ha00] give a deterministic $O(n\alpha(m,n))$ algorithm, where $\alpha(m,n)$ is 
the inverse Ackerman function. Pettie and Ramachandran [PR02] give a provably o
ptimal algorithm whose exact running time is (paradoxically) unknown, but lies 
between $\Omega(n+m)$ and $O(n\alpha(m,n))$. 
