hat offers an effective compromise between two competing network objectives. To
 be precise, $S(G)$ must have total weight close to the MST of $G$ while guaran
teeing that the shortest path between vertices $x$ and $y$ in $S(G)$ approaches
 the shortest path in the full graph $G$. The monograph of Narasimhan and Smid 
[NS07] provides a complete, up-to-date survey on spanner networks. 
