teen vertices. The sheer amount of ink needed to draw any large, dense graph wi
ll overwhelm even a massive display. A drawing of the complete graph on 100 ver
tices $\left(K_{100}\right)$ contains approximately 5,000 edges. On a $1,000 \t
imes 1,000$ pixel display, this works out to 200 pixels per edge. What can you 
hope to see, except a black blob in the center of the screen? 
 []


