[]\T1/lmtt/m/it/10 \item \emph{Radial embeddings}  Free trees are better drawn 
using a radial embedding, where the center of the tree is placed in the center 
of the drawing. The space around this center vertex is divided into angular sec
tors for each subtree. Although the same problem of cramping will eventually oc
cur, radial embeddings make better use of space than ranked embeddings and appe
ar considerably more natural for free trees. 
 []


