ur is a fast and effective way to improve any other heuristic. Experiments sugg
est that 3-optimal tours are usually within a few percent of optimal cost. For 
$k>3$, the computation time increases considerably faster than the solution qua
lity. Simulated annealing provides an alternate mechanism to employ edge flips 
to improve heuristic tours. 
