[]\T1/lmtt/m/it/10 \textbf{Discussion}: Vertex coloring arises in scheduling an
d clustering applications. Register allocation in compiler optimization is the 
canonical application of coloring. Each variable in a given program fragment ha
s a range of times during which its value must be kept intact: in particular, a
fter it is initialized and before its final use. Any two variables whose life s
pans intersect cannot be placed in the same register. Construct a graph where e
ach vertex corresponds to a variable, with an edge between any two vertices who
se variable life spans intersect. If we color the vertices of this graph, we en
sure that no variables assigned the same color will clash. Thus, they all can b
e assigned to the same register. 
