[]\T1/lmtt/m/it/10 \item \textit{Is the graph planar, or are all vertices of lo
w degree?} -- The famous four-color theorem states that every planar graph can 
be vertex colored using at most four distinct colors. Efficient algorithms to f
our-color planar graphs are known, although it is NP-complete to decide whether
 a given planar graph is three-colorable. 
