ssible conflicts, but it is less wasteful to hold non-conflicting events simult
aneously. We construct a graph $G$ whose vertices are people, and whose edges r
epresent the pairs of people who must meet. An edge coloring of $G$ defines the
 schedule, with the color classes representing the different time periods in th
e schedule, so that all meetings of the same color happen simultaneously. 
