[]\T1/lmtt/m/it/10 What exactly is meant when we say that two graphs are the sa
me? Two labeled graphs $G=\left(V_{g}, E_{g}\right)$ and $H=\left(V_{h}, E_{h}\
right)$ are \emph{identical} when $(x, y) \in E_{g}$ iff $(x, y) \in E_{h}$. In
 identical graphs, $v_{i}$ in $G$ corresponds to $v_{i}$ in $H$. The more chall
enging isomorphism problem seeks to find a mapping from the vertices of $G$ to 
$H$ such that they are identical. The problem of finding this mapping is someti
mes called \emph{graph matching}.\index{acyclic subgraph}\index{constraint elim
ination}\index{feedback edge/vertex set} 
