[]\T1/lmtt/m/it/10 This Graham scan procedure can also be used to construct a n
on-selfintersecting (or \textit{simple}) polygon passing through all the points
. Sort the points around \textit{v}, but instead of testing angles, connect the
 points in angular order. This gives a polygon without self-intersection, altho
ugh it typically has many ugly skinny protrusions. 
 []


