Overfull \hbox (2416.49197pt too wide) in paragraph at lines 14379--14379
[]\T1/lmtt/m/it/10 One common technique is to approximate the objects in a scen
e by simpler objects that enclose them, such as boxes. Whenever two enclosing b
oxes intersect, then the underlying objects \textit{might} intersect, and so fu
rther work is necessary to decide the issue. But it is much more efficient to t
est whether simple boxes intersect than more complicated objects, so we win whe
n collisions are rare. Many variations on this theme are possible, but this ide
a leads to large performance improvements for complicated environments. 
