[]\T1/lmtt/m/it/10 \textbf{Discussion}: Bin packing arises in many packaging an
d manufacturing problems. Suppose that you are manufacturing widgets cut from s
heet metal or pants cut from cloth. To minimize cost and waste, we seek to lay 
out the parts to use as few fixed-size metal sheets or bolts of cloth as possib
le. Placing each part on a given sheet, in the best location, is a bin-packing 
variant called the \textit{cutting stock} problem. After our widgets have been 
successfully manufactured, we face another bin-packing problem---how best to fi
t the boxes onto trucks so as to minimize the number of vehicles needed to ship
 everything. 
 []


