[]\T1/lmtt/m/it/10 Even the most elementary-sounding bin-packing problems are N
P-complete; see the discussion of integer partition in Section 16.10 (page 497)
. Thus, we are doomed to think in terms of heuristics, instead of worst-case op
timal algorithms. Fortunately, relatively simple heuristics tend to work well o
n most bin-packing problems. Further, many applications have peculiar, problem-
specific constraints that would frustrate sophisticated algorithms for bin pack
ing. The following factors will affect the choice of heuristic: 
