ff-line} problem)? Or will we get them one at a time and greedily deal with the
m as they arrive (an \emph{on-line} problem)? This difference is important, bec
ause we can do a better job packing when we can take a global view and plan ahe
ad. For example, we can arrange the objects in an order that will facilitate ef
ficient packing, perhaps by sorting them from biggest to smallest. 
