henever the two skeletons are similar enough, we can classify the unknown objec
t as an instance of our model. This technique has proven useful in computer vis
ion and in optical character recognition. The skeleton of a polygon with holes 
(like the letters A and B) is not a tree but an embedded planar graph, yet it r
emains fairly easy to work with. 
