[]\T1/lmtt/m/it/10 Hamming distance is particularly simple and efficient to com
pute on bitmapped images, since after alignment all we do is sum the difference
s of the corresponding pixels. Although Hamming distance makes sense conceptual
ly and can be simple to implement, it captures only a crude notion of shape and
 is likely to be ineffective in many applications. 
