form $y \le a_i x + b_i$. Which point in the plane satisfies the largest number
 of them? Construct the arrangement of the lines. All points in any region or \
emph{cell} of this arrangement will satisfy exactly the same set of constraints
, so we only need to test one point per cell to find the global maximum. 
