s changes to a document. \textit{Cryptographic hash functions} such as MD5 and 
SHA-256 are easy to compute for a given document, but hard to invert. This mean
s that for a particular hash code value $x$, it is hard to construct a document
 $d$ such that $H(d)=x$. The property makes them valuable for digital signature
s and other applications. 
