eterministic machines} -- DFAs are simple to work with, because the machine is 
always in exactly one state at any given time. \textit{Non-deterministic finite
 automata} (NFAs) can be in multiple states at a time, so their current \TS1/lm
tt/m/it/10 ``\T1/lmtt/m/it/10 state\TS1/lmtt/m/it/10 '' \T1/lmtt/m/it/10 repres
ents a subset of the possible machine states. 
